These constants are derived from (UF); they are not imported ray data. Work factorwise in this coefficient algebra. For m=2,4,5 it is a quadratic field over Q, so its two embeddings cover the two geometric roots. For m=3 the factors d=1 and d=-1 are handled separately.

Starting from `p*x^(2m)`, solve rows `2m+j` in decreasing order `j=2m-1,...,2`. Their pivots are

```
A_j=2*(2m+j-3)*p+3/2
   =(2m+j+6d)/(2*(2d+1)).
