+**5.3 Composition and root allocation.** On B=eta=0, if additionally `P in k(L)`, then P is a polynomial in L: a finite pole of a reduced rational expression in L would pull back to a pole under the nonconstant polynomial L. Degree comparison then gives `P=f(L)` with f quadratic. Equation (UF) implies
